thoughts.description:
I'm now investigating a static factory method approach for `JavaScriptDimFilter` to control the instantiation process. The goal is to move the construction logic out of the standard constructor and into a method annotated with `@JsonCreator`. This method will accept all parameters *except* `config`, which will be injected using `@JacksonInject`. The current implementation has a problem with the static factory method not supporting instance values with `@JacksonInject`.
```java
@JsonCreator
public static JavaScriptDimFilter create(
    @JsonProperty("dimension") String dimension,
    @JsonProperty("function") String function,
    @JsonProperty("extractionFn") @Nullable ExtractionFn extractionFn,
    @JsonProperty("filterTuning") @Nullable FilterTuning filterTuning,
    @JacksonInject JavaScriptConfig config
) {
    return new JavaScriptDimFilter(dimension, function, extractionFn, filterTuning, config);
}
```
This is because a static method won't work.

